plaso.tsv.gz: what plaso (the log2timeline/plaso:20260720 Docker image) reads
from tests/fixtures/plaso/SysEvent.Evt with its winevt parser, one line per
event (two per record: the time generated, as "creation", and the time
written), sorted: offset, record number, which time, the time (Unix seconds),
event identifier, message identifier, facility, severity, event type,
category, source name, computer name, user SID, number of strings, the
strings. Written from plaso's output, not from this crate.

With SysEvent.Evt copied to /tmp/smo/evt/in/SysEvent.Evt:

    sudo docker run --rm -v /tmp/smo/evt:/data log2timeline/plaso:20260720 log2timeline --status_view none -q --parsers 'winevt' --storage-file /data/out.plaso /data/in
    sudo docker run --rm -v /tmp/smo/evt:/data log2timeline/plaso:20260720 psort --status_view none -q -o json_line -w /data/out.jsonl /data/out.plaso
    python3 -I tests/oracle/plaso_tsv.py out.jsonl > tests/oracle/plaso.tsv
    gzip -9n tests/oracle/plaso.tsv
